1
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,920
The ultimate harem

2
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,960
Lightly leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:37,420
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,360
I wanna time with you forever

5
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:42,160
Nothing but the latest trends

6
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,080
So you can wear them as you go

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,120
Because your natural face
is what sells out instantly

8
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it ring

9
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:58,220
Everybody can do. The dreams we set off chasing never stop,
you know

10
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:03,580
Let's go out tomorrow without regrets,
love war

11
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:10,820
Everybody can do.
Even if you stray a little, it doesn't hurt

12
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:18,180
Carrying restless curiosity,
stretch far, high and strong

13
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,060
Good morning.

14
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:37,520
Good morning.

15
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,180
Good morning, good morning.

16
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,980
Ryotsu, what's with that outfit?

17
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,420
I was just about to head out on patrol.

18
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,980
Since when did you become
a mountain patrolman?

19
00:01:52,560 --> 00:02:01,660
It's dangerous out there, so I can't patrol without this much gear.
No matter how much I ask, he won't tell me.

20
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:12,980
The preparations are done, so are we about to leave? Go straight down this road.
Go on ahead for a bit.

21
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:14,220
I'll catch up right away.

22
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,640
Ryotsu, what's going on?

23
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:20,300
Hey, isn't that Shuzaburo Himeji over there?

24
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:24,140
Shuzaburo Himeji, the famous archaeologist?

25
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:27,980
Didn't he dig up Akagi-san
with a bulldozer last year?

26
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:30,640
He tried to excavate Tokugawa's buried gold.

27
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,340
It ended in failure, though.

28
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:35,600
Well, time to head out on patrol.

29
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:40,860
Ryo-chan, you're not planning to go searching
for buried gold with that guy, are you?

30
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:46,260
Buried gold?
Are you scheming up another worthless thing?

31
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:49,060
Worthless? How rude.

32
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:52,660
I'd prefer you call it a man's dream,
a man's dream.

33
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:54,860
What man's dream?

34
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:59,020
People should work honestly and live honestly.
That's best.

35
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:04,060
Hunting for buried gold, chasing a fortune like that,
isn't what a man should do.

36
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:09,200
Senpai, buried gold isn't
something you find that easily.

37
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:11,360
That's the way it is.

38
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,300
Well then, Shogun.

39
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:13,520
Leave the rest to you, okay?

40
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,200
Wait.

41
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,100
Wait up, Ryotsu!

42
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:18,880
Honestly, that man...

43
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,860
If it's something that could make money,

44
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,240
he'll do anything for it.

45
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,760
But does it really exist?

46
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,180
No one has ever discovered it.

47
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:28,800
A castle, of all things.

48
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,660
We have no choice but to
trust the ancient documents.

49
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:33,620
Hello.

50
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:34,640
Hello.

51
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:37,000
Hello, hello.

52
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:38,200
Look.

53
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,900
Look at all these samurai!

54
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,460
That's why it's the Phantom Castle.

55
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:45,320
Deep in the mountains of Kai,
a castle stands unseen by anyone.

56
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,580
It's called the Phantom Castle.

57
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:50,200
Atop its peak, a pair of shachi

58
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,900
glitter with golden scales.

59
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,400
Real orcas don't have scales, though.

60
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,700
Originally,
shachihoko were imaginary monsters

61
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,580
modeled after orcas.

62
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:05,220
Placed on both ends of a building's ridge,
they're said to protect it from fire.

63
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:07,180
Trivia like that doesn't matter, though.

64
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:11,080
Are those shachihoko
really made of pure gold?

65
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:14,340
Yeah, Kai Province had gold mines.

66
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:17,160
It says they were made by melting
down a huge number of ōban coins.

67
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,740
I'm not that interested in the money, but

68
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:23,740
Well, judging by their size,
the pair must be worth about a billion yen.

69
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,940
W-what? A billion yen?

70
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,040
Why didn't you say so earlier!

71
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:30,600
If that's the case,
we can't waste time dawdling here.

72
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,140
Let's find the castle quickly.

73
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,920
All I want is to discover Takeda
Shingen's hidden stronghold.

74
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,980
This road isn't on the navigation.

75
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:44,100
Which way?

76
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,060
This way.

77
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,540
Is this road really the right one?

78
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,880
No doubt about it.

79
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,280
It matches the old document exactly.

80
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,600
What is this?

81
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:05,000
This looks like one of
Shingen's hidden hot springs.

82
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,580
Hey, hey,
we're not looking for a hot spring resort!

83
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:16,460
You don't mean that
shachihoko thing, do you?

84
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:17,680
No, no.

85
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:22,700
That's strange, a hot spring
resort like this isn't on the map.

86
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:26,060
Geez, this is going to be a rough ride.

87
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:29,640
Look, see? There really is a road.

88
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,400
After all, the old document was right.

89
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:39,540
It's a dead end!

90
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,260
This old document is totally unreliable.

91
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:48,152
Maybe it's like this...

92
00:05:48,202 --> 00:05:49,200
or maybe...

93
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,160
Let me take a look at it.

94
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,600
Hey, stop! What are you doing?

95
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:56,500
This document is a valuable find
that I struggled to discover, so

96
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:57,940
Just hand it over.

97
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:58,720
No way.

98
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,680
Hand it over.

99
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,440
No.

100
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:16,620
Are you okay?

101
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,220
Looks like we're all right, at least.

102
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:22,500
But we really tumbled down a long way,
didn't we?

103
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:27,380
Still, that saved us quite a bit of time.

104
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,560
Don't make me laugh.

105
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:31,780
There's a house over there!

106
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:33,940
Looks like a teahouse.

107
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,400
Let's take a little break here.

108
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:43,040
Welcome, welcome!

109
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,460
Shall we get some tea and dumplings?

110
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:51,200
Where are you all headed, then?

111
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:55,100
Actually,
we're looking for something around here.

112
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,560
Something you're looking for

113
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,340
And what exactly might it be?

114
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:05,560
Nothing.
We were just hiking and got a little lost.

115
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:06,720
Right?

116
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,500
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

117
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,260
But you know,

118
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:15,780
no one's going to come to
a teahouse way out here.

119
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:17,002
Well,

120
00:07:17,052 --> 00:07:21,643
every now and then,
lost travelers like you do come by.

121
00:07:21,693 --> 00:07:22,740
No need to worry.

122
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:23,980
Ha I see.

123
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,320
After you eat the dumplings,
he said to go down this way,

124
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:34,080
and if you walk a while,
you'll hit a mountain trail.

125
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,920
What do we do, Ryo-san?

126
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:42,080
My gut says it's definitely up ahead.

127
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,900
I can smell gold up ahead.

128
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,720
Sorry, I just farted.

129
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,680
Ugh.

130
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,420
Gramps,
I'll leave the money for the tea here.

131
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,920
Keep the change.

132
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,860
Hold on a second.

133
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:00,920
What's this supposed to be?
This thousand yen?

134
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,720
What, was that too much?

135
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,780
Don't you dare joke around like that!

136
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,475
Tea is five hundred yen a cup, and
dumplings are a thousand yen for three sticks,

137
00:08:09,525 --> 00:08:11,600
so for the two of you,
it's three thousand yen total.

138
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,680
You'll pay up in full.

139
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,520
It was three thousand yen?

140
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:19,900
Damn it, what a old geezer,
taking advantage of customers like this.

141
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:24,200
Yeah, there's no electricity, gas, or running
water out here in the middle of the mountains.

142
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,920
Even three thousand yen doesn't cover it.

143
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:33,120
there,

144
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,920
well, thanks as always.

145
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,520
Do come again.

146
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,880
Like I'd ever come back!

147
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,440
No, no, not that way. You can't go that way.

148
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,620
I told you the mountain trail is that way,
didn't I?

149
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,580
Beyond here, the snow stops you cold.

150
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:50,160
Go in there without permission
and you'll be cursed!

151
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,280
A curse?

152
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,200
How ridiculous.

153
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,220
Come on, move aside.

154
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,960
So this really is the snowline

155
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:11,240
Yeah, it's just like that
old man Bottakure said.

156
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:16,540
I'm sure the Phantom
Castle is somewhere nearby.

157
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,800
There's no way we can climb this rock wall.

158
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:24,040
Might as well take a leak while we're here.

159
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,440
It's frustrating,
but we have no choice but to turn back.

160
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:32,980
What's wrong?

161
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:34,440
Come here for a second.

162
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,980
What, can't you even
take a piss by yourself?

163
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:40,230
Of course I can. That's not it, though.

164
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,680
Try pouring some water right here.

165
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,140
Just cover it with sand or something.

166
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:45,380
I'm not a cat.

167
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,120
Like this?

168
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:56,840
Hear that?
You can hear the water running away.

169
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,780
Yeah, there seems to
be something underneath.

170
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:03,140
But there's no way we
can move a rock this big.

171
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:04,780
Whoa, it moved!

172
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,560
What's this? Pumice?

173
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,200
Ryo-san, there really is something here!

174
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,340
Look, the light from the exit!

175
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,100
Whoa, it's a castle! A castle!

176
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,740
It's the Phantom Castle.

177
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:37,740
We did it! The golden shachihoko!

178
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,640
We found it! We finally found it!

179
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,820
But you know, normally a castle

180
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,640
is built so it looks down over the lowlands,
isn't it?

181
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,840
This one looks more like a hideout.

182
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,160
That's exactly why it's a phantom castle.

183
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,960
The lord, a descendant of the Shinen line,
was a thorough misanthrope,

184
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,980
so he built his castle in this remote place,
far from the world.

185
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,520
With this, it's no wonder no
one has found it until now.

186
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:09,460
But how do we get to it?

187
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,720
There's no bridge anywhere around here.

188
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:17,980
It says here we enter through the main gate,
using bridge and bridge,

189
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:19,340
Bridge and bridge?

190
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,820
Could it be that?

191
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,680
This won't reach, damn it.

192
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,580
How about using another one?

193
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,320
They're the same length.

194
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:35,060
Using another one would still
be the same thing, though.

195
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,680
Wait a minute...

196
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,160
Use the ends of both.

197
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,600
Got it.

198
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:44,120
That way, we can cross over.

199
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,040
I see.

200
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:49,420
So the meaning was to use the end
of the tree and the end of the bird.

201
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:57,080
"Do not open this gate,"

202
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,760
*clank clank clank*

203
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:04,680
Mm...

204
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:05,900
*ugh*

205
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:07,460
*grr*

206
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:08,320
Damn it!

207
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,540
It really won't open.

208
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:10,680
It's been like this all along.

209
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:11,180
*clunk*

210
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:12,420
Seriously.

211
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:13,940
Putting up a useless sign like that!

212
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,960
And now it's a huge iron gate!

213
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:19,880
Rattle, rattle, rattle!

214
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:23,720
No matter how hard I push or pull,
it won't budge!

215
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:27,720
"When the Tatsumi meets the horse,
the gate shall open."

216
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,600
A code

217
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:31,300
Then this statue must be the hint.

218
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,080
But that's strange,
there's no horse anywhere.

219
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,700
Doesn't "horse" refer to a direction?

220
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:41,340
In the Edo period,
"horse" was a word for south.

221
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:44,500
That's it!
We turn the Tatsumi statue to the south.

222
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,660
So what exactly is "Tatsumi"?

223
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:51,260
Tatsumi refers to the Edo
dragon and snake, my boy.

224
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:53,520
Right, so the dragon
and the snake face south.

225
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,700
Which way is south?

226
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:59,400
The navi won't get a
signal out here, though.

227
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,920
Right, let's try that method.

228
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,960
What are we supposed to do,
cutting down a tree?

229
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,480
We look at the cut surface, of course.

230
00:13:06,940 --> 00:13:09,800
The side with the wider
growth rings is south.

231
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:12,380
That way! Let's look at the Tatsu!

232
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,320
And then, a snake.

233
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,660
That's not a snake, it's a statue.

234
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:26,140
Who made such a ridiculous statue, damn it.

235
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,320
Alright, we have to be much more careful.

236
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:33,000
Yeah, anyway, the gate opened,
so no complaints, right?

237
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,940
Hmph, that man has finally
made it all the way here.

238
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:47,860
Looks like my time has finally come.

239
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:51,400
For over 400 long years,

240
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:55,280
we of the Maboroshi clan have
guarded this castle eternally.

241
00:13:57,140 --> 00:14:03,680
Now only I remain, but I won't
lose to you young whippersnappers.

242
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,760
I'll show those intruders what's what.

243
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:33,260
This place really feels
like a haunted mansion.

244
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:36,520
Well, it's been standing
for hundreds of years.

245
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:40,060
Well, I've got no complaints
as long as I get my cut.

246
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:43,040
Anyway, we just have to climb
all the way to the top floor.

247
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,800
If we go that way...

248
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:53,280
Watch out, there's a falling-ceiling trap.

249
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,800
Then say so sooner!

250
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:59,220
The traps are still working perfectly,
even now.

251
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:01,500
No telling what kind of traps there are.

252
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,900
Alright, second floor!

253
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:11,020
Damn, this staircase is like
something out of a comedy sketch.

254
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:13,020
We can't get through like this.

255
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:17,440
I'll make you suffer, I'll make you suffer.

256
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,320
Hngh

257
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:21,500
Hngh

258
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:21,520
Hngh

259
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:21,640
Hngh

260
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:21,720
Hngh

261
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:21,800
Hngh

262
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,000
Alright, come on up!

263
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,400
This is just the start.

264
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:34,580
What?!

265
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:38,960
Not nearly enough!

266
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:43,840
How about this?

267
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,900
The traps are getting serious now

268
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,280
This had better be worth at
least ten golden shachihoko.

269
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,820
Says the gold-obsessed man.

270
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:07,260
Then it's on to the next move.

271
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,680
Finally, the third floor.

272
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:15,120
The top floor is the fifth,
so we're only halfway there.

273
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,600
Anyway, let's go look for the stairs.

274
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:21,600
What's that?

275
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,440
There's something written inside it!

276
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:25,960
Bound for the top floor?

277
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:29,860
Could this possibly be an elevator?

278
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,820
Hey, hey, isn't this another trap?

279
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:35,860
An old gold coin, right here!

280
00:16:35,860 --> 00:16:36,820
What?

281
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:40,440
Thought so, but it's just a brass plate.

282
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,980
Hey, no good!

283
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:50,760
Who are you?

284
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:55,960
I thought you had some backbone,
but you're still wet behind the ears.

285
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,520
You're the rip-off old
geezer from the teahouse.

286
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,800
Who're you calling a rip-off old geezer?

287
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,880
We have no use for fools blinded by greed.

288
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:09,000
Just let us out of here already!

289
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:13,860
Since you've broken into this castle, guarded
by the Maboroshi clan, without permission,

290
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:16,580
we can't let you out of there.

291
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,140
Maboroshi clan?

292
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:19,580
That's right, the Maboroshi.

293
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:23,840
Your aim is the golden shachihoko,
I presume.

294
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:28,440
But as long as I'm here, it's impossible
for you to lay a single finger on it.

295
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:33,120
Is that so? I could do more than touch it with one finger.
I could nuzzle it cheek to cheek!

296
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:35,080
Quite the confidence you have.

297
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:40,100
Then if you can touch it,
I'll give you the golden shachihoko.

298
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:43,180
Though that's assuming you can get out of there,
that is.

299
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:48,760
You stink!
Don't you forget what you just said!

300
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,400
What's this supposed to be?

301
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:55,060
What a guy!

302
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:57,820
With this, then...

303
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,520
Whoaaaaaa!

304
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,360
This is bad!

305
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:03,340
Noooooo!

306
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:05,300
Aaaaaaah!

307
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,960
Aaaaaaah!

308
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,420
Aaaaaaah!

309
00:18:08,370 --> 00:18:11,760
Damn it, we're back to square one again.

310
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:13,820
Aaaaaaah!

311
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,660
Both of you, give up already.

312
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,580
I'll never give up!

313
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:18,080
Aaaaaaah!

314
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:21,160
That old man said we could
have it too if we touched it.

315
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,560
The one-billion-yen shachihoko.

316
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,520
Well then,
let's gratefully accept it, shall we?

317
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,880
W-what?!

318
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:40,400
That it would reach all the way up there!

319
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,400
Nothing is impossible for me.

320
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:45,160
Maboroshi clan or whatever it is,

321
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:49,040
if you won't let us climb from inside,
we'll climb from outside!

322
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:51,440
We should've done this from the start!

323
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:56,760
Hey, Ryo-san, be careful!

324
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,120
Alright, one more push!

325
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:07,720
Well, you've made it this far.
I'll give you credit.

326
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:10,960
Back again, are you? How diligent of you.

327
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,760
Enough games. It ends here!

328
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:18,240
Huh? The sword won't come out?

329
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,860
Gah! Did my body go stiff?

330
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:21,480
No!

331
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,620
Ugh, I can't keep up with this.

332
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:23,880
Hey, wait!

333
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:25,420
Right, now's our chance.

334
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,620
Whoa, damn it!

335
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:32,940
Ninpo: Katon no jutsu!
This is the final blow!

336
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:40,180
Haah!

337
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,180
Don't set that up right in front of me!

338
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:44,920
Alright, go!

339
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:48,357
Damn, those movements,

340
00:19:48,407 --> 00:19:50,860
he's no ordinary man.

341
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,180
Could he be a Uesugi ninja?

342
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:58,740
Yay, golden shachihoko-chan!

343
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:00,000
Stop it!

344
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:05,620
You mustn't touch that shachihoko!

345
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:09,200
What are you talking about? We had a
deal that whoever touches it gets it!

346
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,400
Either way, you must not touch it!

347
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:15,320
Shut up,
what I do with my property is my business!

348
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,620
Figures! I said you mustn't!

349
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:21,520
Here goes! Got it!

350
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,740
Too late!

351
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:30,960
It's over.

352
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:33,460
I understand you're frustrated,

353
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:37,320
but even without a shachihoko, there's a
magnificent castle, so it's fine, isn't it?

354
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:38,800
What?

355
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:43,540
Taking the shachihoko makes the whole castle collapse.
That's how it's rigged.

356
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:44,520
What?

357
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:50,200
Make sure this golden shachihoko
never falls into anyone's hands.

358
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:53,640
What on earth just happened?

359
00:20:57,520 --> 00:21:00,680
Now that it's come to this,
no one can stop it.

360
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:05,000
I'll give you the golden
shachihoko as promised.

361
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:07,160
What?

362
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:33,340
You showed real promise.

363
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:35,440
Farewell.

364
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,420
Well, this has truly become a phantom.

365
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:06,600
Nobody's going to believe us now.

366
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,260
But we've got this!

367
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:17,940
See? Didn't I tell you?

368
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:20,700
This whole shachihoko is all mine.

369
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:23,960
Everyone,
go ahead and feast your eyes on it.

370
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:25,680
Especially you, Chief.

371
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:29,140
Living honestly, you'd never get to see
anything like this in your whole life.

372
00:22:29,940 --> 00:22:32,660
That's just something I
bought at some souvenir shop.

373
00:22:32,660 --> 00:22:34,560
It's obviously a plated fake.

374
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,460
Ugh, how disgusting.
That's just how poor people are.

375
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:41,540
Just look at this luster, this shine.

376
00:22:41,540 --> 00:22:44,620
How on earth is this fake plating...

377
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:48,720
Listen!
We've been banging it against everything.

378
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:51,560
Oh my, the base metal's showing, Ryo-chan.

379
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:52,920
W-what?

380
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:56,180
T-this really is just plating!

381
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:58,240
No, no, no, no...

382
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:07,440
And judging by that cheap sheen, the plating itself isn't much good either.
That's just like you, Mr. President.

383
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:09,860
Nn... d...

384
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,280
It's Kenya!

385
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:23,260
With this old man, he's totally letchy.

386
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:25,880
I'm not some old man!

387
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:28,520
Call me "uncle," call me uncle!

388
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:31,400
Still, "big brother" is better.

389
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,580
Hee, that's impossible.

390
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:36,280
Yeah, calling you "big brother"...

391
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:38,340
I see, I see.

392
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:41,460
So this is a "no touching" then, is it?

393
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:44,240
Eek! Eek! Eek!

394
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:45,540
Big brother!

395
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:48,900
Now that the white's gone,
I feel much better.

396
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:51,740
The rest of your life is best spent happily.

397
00:23:51,940 --> 00:23:54,080
Nyahahahahaha.

398
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:56,640
Hey, hey, want this?

399
00:23:56,980 --> 00:23:57,900
I want it!

400
00:23:58,580 --> 00:24:00,280
Eek! That's scary!

401
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,534
What a real shame, what a pity.

402
00:24:06,584 --> 00:24:10,420
Once you're done cleaning,
go buy some beer and sukiyaki beef.

403
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:14,480
What's that? You're asking if it's all right
to eat such worldly things during training?

404
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:18,400
Don't worry, don't worry.
Just leave it to this priest, Ryotsu.

405
00:24:18,740 --> 00:24:21,820
Next time: Ryotsu, currently in training.
See you then.

406
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:32,660
Even if we stop the clocks,

407
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps moving on,

408
00:24:39,340 --> 00:24:42,660
so with a scowl and tears,

409
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:48,000
let's laugh it off and keep on living.

410
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

411
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,940
is a rainy day,

412
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

413
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:13,800
Bye-bye, let's wave,
goodbye to the bad stuff.

414
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:23,960
Oh yeah, live however you like,
good things are coming.

415
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:30,260
Outside the door, the star is calling you.

416
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:40,920
Thank you for watching.

